2026-08-16T14:33:58Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: The combination step is on the wrong basis: you state “a weighted median is undefined for two values, so submitted their weighted midpoint,” but a weighted median is defined and, with your inputs, equals the lower candidate. Sorted by value, 4.40315 has weight 0.928 and 6.75971 has weight 0.072; the cumulative weight crosses 0.5 at 4.40315, so the weighted median is 4.40315, not the midpoint 4.57391. Using the midpoint lifts the estimate by ~3.9% despite 92.8% of the weight pointing to 4.40315.
2026-08-16T14:34:00Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic (not concrete, no action): You projected FY2026Q2 by simply applying the FY2024Q2→FY2025Q2 YoY rate (+4.86%) to the FY2025Q2 base, ignoring Home Depot’s published FY2026 outlook/consensus for sales (which was flat to low single-digit at best). That’s a basis error: using a backward-looking single-quarter growth rate as a like-for-like proxy instead of anchoring to FY2026 guidance/consensus likely overstates the quarter’s net sales.
2026-08-16T14:34:19Z    [ADI:Revenue] GATE critic: The weighted blend is miscalculated: 3900 × 0.967 + 3112.9 × 0.033 = 3874.03 USDm, not 3873.91 USDm. Your submitted value is off by about 0.12 USDm.
