2026-08-16T14:34:57Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: The decision rule is wrong: a weighted median with two values is not “undefined.” With 4.59209 (weight 0.889) and 4.68251 (weight 0.111), the weighted median is 4.59209 (the point where cumulative weight first exceeds 50%). By switching to a weighted mean (4.60214), you changed the estimator and pushed the figure up by about $0.010, which would alter the rounded EPS from $4.59 to $4.60. The reported 4.60214 is therefore on the wrong basis relative to the stated median-aggregation approach.
2026-08-16T14:35:06Z    [ADI:Adjusted gross margin] GATE critic: You anchored on FY2025Q3 “69.2%” as the prior-year adjusted gross margin, but that appears to be the GAAP figure. Your own source line for FY2025Q3 shows “69.2 % | 67.9 % | 130 bps,” which, consistent with the other rows (e.g., FY2024Q3 “67.9% | 72.2%”), reads as GAAP | Adjusted | Δ. The correct adjusted prior-year anchor should be 67.9%, not 69.2%, so the 70.03% blend (and thus 70.375%) is built on the wrong basis.
