2026-08-16T14:35:53Z    [HAS:Net fees] GATE critic: Your core YoY decline (-13.17%) is internally inconsistent with the inputs you cite: the weights 0.62 and 0.37 sum to 0.99, and applying them to -12.7% and -14.0% yields about -13.05%, not -13.17%. Using the stated weights would give a higher FY2026 base (~£845.5m before the tilt) and, after the -1.42% tilt, about £833.4m, not £832.4m. This arithmetic/weighting error makes the proposed £832.396m too low.
