2026-08-16T14:36:21Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional basic EPS] GATE critic: You used a 35.1% tax rate in the FY26 EPS calculation, but management guides to an FY26 ETR of about 45%. Applying the guided 45% to your P&L inputs gives: (45.47 – 13.4) × (1 – 0.45) ÷ 1,590.2m × 100 ≈ 1.11 GBp, not 1.309 GBp. Using 35.1% (FY25) for FY26 is the wrong period/basis and overstates EPS.
2026-08-16T14:36:57Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional operating profit] GATE critic: Your own source lists FY2026 pre-exceptional operating profit guidance at £45.2m, yet your “guidance_anchor+signal” input is 46.104—about £0.9m higher than the cited guidance. Given you weight this anchor at 96.9%, using the documented £45.2m would pull the blend down to roughly £44.57m, not £45.47m. The submitted figure is thus inconsistent with the stated guidance and is likely too high.
